[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Sold Out]
[00:00.86]When will the writer see the play? | 作者什么时候会看这部戏？
[00:14.08]'The play may begin at any moment,' I said. | “这出戏随时都可能开始，”我说。
[00:19.32]'It may have begun already,' Susan answered. | “可能已经开始了，”苏珊回答说。
[00:24.03]I hurried to the ticket office. | 我赶紧跑到售票处。
[00:27.34]'May I have two tickets please?' I asked. | “请给我两张票好吗？”我问道。
[00:32.05]'I'm sorry, we've sold out,' the girl said. | “对不起，票已经卖完了，”那个女孩说。
[00:36.70]'What a pity!' Susan exclaimed. | “真可惜！”苏珊惊呼道。
[00:41.08]Just then, a man hurried to the ticket office. | 就在那时，一个男人匆匆跑到售票处。
[00:46.12]'Can I return these two tickets?' he asked. | “我能退这两张票吗？”他问道。
[00:50.77]'Certainly,' the girl said. | “当然可以，”那个女孩说。
[00:54.44]I went back to the ticket office at once. | 我立刻回到了售票处。
[00:58.91]'Could I have those two tickets please?' I asked. | “我能要那两张票吗？”我问道。
[01:04.60]'Certainly,' the girl said, | “当然可以，”那个女孩说，
[01:08.28]'but they're for next Wednesday's performance. | “但那是下周三演出的票。
[01:12.05]Do you still want them?' | 你还要吗？”
[01:14.89]'I might as well have them,' I said sadly. | “我还是把它们拿走吧，”我伤心地说。